Z||000000||MontanaFiero||08-13-2001||01:20 PM||||On my '86 2.8L there is a sensor that is in the upper left hand corner of the head, right under the ignition coil that broke when I was trying to remove the plug.  My manuals say nothing about what this sensor is, although I have a feeling it is a temp sensor of some sort.  The connector also broke--it is square and has two green wires in it. Anybody know what this is?<BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||08-13-2001||01:24 PM||||coolant temp  fan switch.. if you wire throught it the fan comes on all the time andthe car freeks out cause it swears it's to hot.. NAPA has them for $12 5280 Southgate Dr., Billings..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and the accompanying plug to go with it... AND heat reflective tape too! ||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||08-13-2001||02:11 PM||||I think he means on the transmission side 1fst, under the coil is the Coolant Temperature sending unit to gauge. Fan switch is on top of intake by radiator fill cap.||||reg||1
Z||000003||MontanaFiero||08-13-2001||03:29 PM||||OKAY 1FST2M6, you are starting to scare me now   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> hehe-- can you tell me where the carquest is too? (yeah I remember, your fiance grew up here, right?)<P>anyway, Roger is right, about the location, but mine is in the head, kinda angled down into the head from the corner. At least I know what it is called now. <P>1FST2M6-- do u think I can get that connector too?  Look me up if you ever get up here to visit the in-laws <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by MontanaFiero (edited 08-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||08-13-2001||07:49 PM||||yes that is the coolant temp sending unit in the top corner of the head. If you cant get the connector at your dealer, Im pretty sure Fiero Store has them.. ||||reg||1
